    "family_reading": {
        "text": "MiniMax spans eight catalog versions, from MiniMax-01 in January 2025 to MiniMax M3 in May 2026. Across the family, 6 of 8 versions support reasoning and 6 of 8 publish open weights, so open and closed releases sit side by side. Context windows run from 65536 to 1048576 tokens, and the line takes image, text and video input while returning text only. The newest versions are cheap for their size, with M3 at $0.3 per million input and $1.2 output and a 512000 token output ceiling, while M1 costs more at $0.55 input and $2.2 output. This suits long document, video and image work where low cost per token matters. Limits: M2-her has a 65536 token window and only 2048 output tokens, and M1 caps output at 40000 tokens despite its million token context.",
